flag provided but not defined: -policy
usage: operate [flags] start|stop|test|scale|autoscale

  -advertise-port int
    	Port this service listens on and advertises
  -client string
    	autoscale load generator: mercury (bin/loadgen as a Mercury daemon) or inproc (this process pinned to CPUs 60-63) (default "mercury")
  -cold-cache
    	leave odd hotel ids uncached so requests still read MongoDB (HOTEL_COLD_CACHE) (default true)
  -config string
    	hotel address file (default "/home/pager/Documents/Mercury/benchmarks/deathstar-hotelReservations/config.json")
  -conns int
    	gRPC connections each route shares among its workers; 0 = one per worker (old behaviour) (default 16)
  -cpu int
    	daemon CPU number Mercury was given (not the CPU Mercury pinned itself to)
  -file string
    	deployment list (default "/home/pager/Documents/Mercury/benchmarks/mercury-hotel.txt")
  -gen-bin string
    	loadgen binary for -client mercury (default "/home/pager/Documents/Mercury/benchmarks/deathstar-hotelReservations/bin/loadgen")
  -gen-cpu int
    	loadgen home Linux CPU (default 60)
  -gen-max int
    	loadgen saturate max cores (default 8)
  -gen-min int
    	loadgen saturate min cores (default 2)
  -gen-out string
    	loadgen output file (default output/loadgen-<unix>.out)
  -gen-procs int
    	loadgen GOMAXPROCS (keep >= gen-max so busy threads can exceed cores) (default 8)
  -mercury string
    	Mercury host:port (default "127.0.0.1:8080")
  -users int
    	maximum concurrent users on each autoscale route (default 1024)
